  <p class="eyebrow">Where most of the work happens</p>
  <h1>IFS-informed EMDR</h1>
  <div class="answer">
    <p>Standard EMDR asks you to hold a memory and let the processing run. For people with
    developmental trauma that instruction often meets an internal objection: a part of you that
    has spent years keeping the material at a distance, and has good reasons.
    <strong>IFS-informed EMDR</strong> treats that objection as information rather than
    resistance. Processing starts when the protective parts agree to it, not when the protocol
    says it is time. This is the focus of Reem Glasco's clinical work, and the reason most
    people arrive here. Sessions are 50 minutes, self-pay, online across
    Texas, with Blue Cross Blue Shield accepted.</p>
  </div>
